    "text": "On manega wisan l\u00e6r\u00f0 Godes lar \u00fea Cristenan.\nOn \u00fe\u00e6re lare is \u00e6g\u00f0er ge li\u00f0nys ge sti\u00f0nyss, for \u00fean \u00f0e ealle men ne magon anes modes beon.\n\u00c6rest man fet \u00fe\u00e6t cild mid meolce, and sy\u00f0\u00f0an mid hlafe.\nGif \u00f0u hit fetst \u00e6rest mid hlafe, hit ne leofa\u00f0 sona.\nEft, \u00feonne hit yldre by\u00f0, hit behofa\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s hlafes, and sti\u00f0ran metes.\nSwa is eac on Godes lare li\u00f0nyss and sti\u00f0nys, \u00fe\u00e6t se \u00f0e gyt ne m\u00e6g \u00fea m\u00e6stan beboda healdan, \u00fe\u00e6t he\nAn eor\u00f0lic cyning h\u00e6f\u00f0 meniges cynnes menn, sume ge\u00feungenran, sume unge\u00feungenran.\nSwa gedafena\u00f0 eac Gode \u00fe\u00e6t he gode men h\u00e6bbe and ge\u00feungene \u00feenas to his \u00f0enungum, and him\nPaulus, \u00feeoda lareow, cw\u00e6\u00f0, swylce be him sylfum ac he m\u00e6nde mid \u00feam eac o\u00f0re menn, \u00f0a \u00f0a ic w\u00e6s\nEft, \u00fea \u00fea ic to werlicere ylde becom, ic awearp and aidlode \u00fea idelnyssa \u00fee ic on cildlicre ylde beeode.\nEft cw\u00e6\u00f0 sum witega, Puer centum annorum maledictus erit: Hundteontigwintre cild by\u00f0 awyrged.\n\u00d0\u00e6t is on andgite, Se mann \u00f0e h\u00e6f\u00f0 ylde on gearum, and h\u00e6f\u00f0 cildes \u00feeawas on dysige, \u00fe\u00e6t se by\u00f0\n\u00c6lc treow blew\u00f0 \u00e6r \u00fean \u00fee hit w\u00e6stmas bere, and \u00e6lc corn bi\u00f0 \u00e6rest g\u00e6rs.\nSwa eac \u00e6lc godes cinnes mann sceal hine sylfne to godnysse awendan, and wisdom lufian, and\nHe sceal hlystan wisdomes \u00e6t wisum mannum, for \u00fean swa he oftor Godes lare gehyr\u00f0, swa he\nNe sceal nan mann forhogian \u00fe\u00e6t he gehyre Godes lare, for \u00fean \u00f0e hit by\u00f0 swy\u00f0e pleolic \u00feam men \u00fe\u00e6t\nW\u00e6teres gecynd is hnesce, and stanes gecynd is heard, ac swa\u00feeah \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6ter foroft dropm\u00e6lum \u00feyrla\u00f0\nSwa eac Godes word \u00feurhg\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s mannes heortan, and ahnexa\u00f0 to Godes bebodum, gif he gelome \u00fea\nGod cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00e6t fruman to mancynne, on middaneardes anginne, Weaxa\u00f0 and beo\u00f0 gemenigfylde, and\nEft on \u00fe\u00e6re niwan gecy\u00f0nysse, \u00fe\u00e6t is on godspelbodunge, cw\u00e6\u00f0 Crist to \u00f0am IUdeiscum, Ic secge eow\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6don Cristes leorningcnihtas him to, Gif \u00f0am were is \u00feus mid wife, selre him by\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he ne\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 Crist, Ne underfo\u00f0 ealle men \u00feis word, ac \u00feam \u00fee hit forgifen by\u00f0.\nSume eunuchi synd \u00fee beo\u00f0 swa acennede, and sume eunuchi synd \u00fee synd fram mannum swa\nHealde \u00f0is se \u00fee hit healdan m\u00e6ge.\nGif Crist hete ealle men healdan m\u00e6g\u00f0had, \u00feonne wurde mancyn ra\u00f0e geendod.\nNu is Criste leofre \u00fe\u00e6t se man be his agenre gecorennysse \u00fea cl\u00e6nnysse geceose \u00fee he sylf astealde,\nAnd seo cl\u00e6ne lac, \u00fe\u00e6t is m\u00e6g\u00f0had, sceal beon Gode mid gl\u00e6dnysse geoffrod, na mid neadunge \u00e6nigre\nWite gehwa, se \u00f0e \u00fea cl\u00e6nnysse Gode \u00e6ne beh\u00e6t, \u00fe\u00e6t he hit eft ne aw\u00e6ge.\nF\u00e6der and moder moton heora bearn to swa hwylcum cr\u00e6fte gedon swa him leofost by\u00f0, and God bead\nGif hi \u00feonne heora bearn Gode bet\u00e6ca\u00f0, to his cl\u00e6num \u00f0eowdome, and \u00fe\u00e6t bearn by\u00f0 him\nNe mot nan man his lima ne his gesceapu forceorfan.\nWe r\u00e6da\u00f0 on \u00fe\u00e6re bec, Uita Patrum, \u00fe\u00e6t twegen munecas geh\u00e6ldon hi sylfe ; ac ealle \u00f0a halgan\nGod behet \u00feurh \u00feone witegan Isaiam \u00feam mannum \u00fee on m\u00e6g\u00f0hade wunia\u00f0, and \u00fea cl\u00e6nnysse gecuron\nSe apostol Paulus, ealra \u00feeoda lareow, awrat on his pistole \u00f0us: Ic secge wydewum, and \u00feam \u00f0e butan\nEft cw\u00e6\u00f0 se ylca apostol, Gif \u00f0u wif nimst, \u00feu ne syngast; and gif m\u00e6den ceorla\u00f0, heo ne synga\u00f0.\nIc secge swa\u00feeah \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fees tima is swi\u00f0e sceort.\nBeon for\u00f0i \u00fea \u00f0e wif habba\u00f0 swylce hi nan nabbon; and \u00fea \u00f0e blissia\u00f0 swylce hi na ne blission; and \u00fea\n\u00d0ises middaneardes hiw gewit.\nSe man \u00fee butan wife wuna\u00f0 hoga\u00f0 hu he Gode gecweme; and se \u00fee mid wife wuna\u00f0 hoga\u00f0 embe\nAnd cl\u00e6ne m\u00e6den cep\u00f0 Godes willan, \u00fe\u00e6t heo halig sy \u00e6g\u00f0er ge on lichaman ge on sawle; and seo \u00f0e\n\u00d0\u00e6t wif by\u00f0 under hyre weres iuce \u00fea hwile \u00fee he leofa\u00f0; and gif heo hyre wer oferbit, \u00feonne by\u00f0 heo\nIc wene \u00fe\u00e6t ic h\u00e6bbe Godes Gast on me.\nSe ylca \u00f0eoda lareow, Paulus, cw\u00e6\u00f0: God by\u00f0 \u00feam men \u00fe\u00e6t he wif ne hreppe; swa\u00feeah, \u00fee l\u00e6s \u00fee hi on\nGif hwylc gelyfed man h\u00e6f\u00f0 ungeleafful wif, and heo wylle wunian mid him, ne forl\u00e6te he hi; \u00fe\u00e6t\nAnd gif hwylc geleafful wif h\u00e6f\u00f0 ungeleaffulne wer, and he wylle wunian mid hyre, ne forl\u00e6te heo\nIc bebeode swa\u00f0eah na ic ac God sylf bebyt \u00fe\u00e6t wer and wif hi ne totw\u00e6man.\nGif hi \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6t do\u00f0, wunian hi butan h\u00e6mede, o\u00f0\u00f0e hi eft hi gegaderian.\nEac hit w\u00e6re rihtlic, \u00e6fter boca t\u00e6cinge, \u00fe\u00e6t se cniht ungewemmed w\u00e6re o\u00f0\u00f0\u00e6t he wifode, swa swa\nSe ylca apostol cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00e6lc man h\u00e6f\u00f0 synderlice gife fram Gode, sum swa, sum elles.\nSwa mycel is se sinscipe, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feeah hwa h\u00e6bbe untymende wif, and heo ne mage bearn habban, \u00fe\u00e6t se\nNis swa\u00feeah h\u00e6med geset for nanum \u00feinge buton for bearnes gestreone, and \u00e6fter \u00feam boclican\nSe \u00f0e \u00feis healdan m\u00e6g, he by\u00f0 fulfremed on l\u00e6wedum hade, swa swa we be manegum mannum\nSe \u00f0e hine sylfne to \u00feyssere forh\u00e6fednysse gewyldan ne m\u00e6g, he ah \u00feearfe \u00fe\u00e6t he mid \u00e6lmyssan and\nIs eac to witenne \u00fe\u00e6t Cristene men sceoldon gan to husle oftor \u00feonne hi do\u00f0, swa swa man de\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r\nEawf\u00e6ste men magon gan to husle be Godes leafe Sunnandagum on Lenctenf\u00e6stene, and on \u00f0am \u00ferim\n\u00d0us m\u00e6g don se \u00f0e rihtlice leofa\u00f0, gif he ne by\u00f0 under\u00feeod \u00feam eahta heafodleahtrum: \u00fe\u00e6t is,\nSe \u00fee swa oft gan nelle to husle, gange huru \u00feriwa on geare.\nGif man seocne mann husla\u00f0, he sceal his synna geandettan, and he ne sceal na ortruwian, ne on\nBe \u00f0am we magon secgan sume so\u00f0e bysne, swa swa Beda awrat, \u00f0ysum wordum secgende: He cw\u00e6\u00f0\nSe \u00feegen w\u00e6s gymeleas on his \u00feeawum and d\u00e6dum, and dyslice leofode, and fordyde hine sylfne.\n\u00d0a manode hine se cyning \u00fe\u00e6t he his mand\u00e6da geswice, and his synna geandette mid so\u00f0re\nSe cyning hine lufode, and gelome hine swa tihte, ac he forseah his lare, and let him ea\u00f0e embe \u00fe\u00e6t,\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00f0a gesicelod sarlice \u00e6t nextan, and se cyning Kenred com to him licgendum, and b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he nolde cy\u00f0an \u00fea his synna, ac sy\u00f0\u00f0an he gewyrpte he wolde hi geandettan, \u00fey l\u00e6s \u00f0e\nHim \u00feuhte \u00fe\u00e6t he spr\u00e6ce \u00feegenlice word, ac he w\u00e6s beswicen \u00feurh \u00feone swicolan deofol, swa swa\nHis wise w\u00e6s \u00f0a wyrsigende, and him weox seo untrumnys, and se cyning eode eft in to \u00f0am seocan.\nHe clypode \u00f0a earmlice, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam cyninge, Hw\u00e6t woldest \u00feu nu \u00e6t me?\nNe miht \u00feu me nanum gode.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 se cyning him to, Ne clypa \u00feu swa unwislice; wite \u00fein gewit.\nHe andwyrde and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ne eom ic na gewitleas, ac min gewit is yfel.\nMe comon lytle \u00e6r to twegen Godes englas, and brohton me ane boc, seo w\u00e6s beorhte scinende, ac\nIc \u00f0a sceawode \u00fea boc and \u00fe\u00e6ron geseah \u00fea feawa godan d\u00e6da \u00fee ic dyde seldon, \u00fea w\u00e6ron swy\u00f0e\nEfne \u00fea f\u00e6rlice comon \u00fea cwealmb\u00e6ran deoflu, swy\u00f0e an\u00fer\u00e6c werod, and eall \u00f0is hus afyldon, and\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a se fyrmesta for\u00f0teah ane boc mycele and orm\u00e6te, swylce mannes byr\u00f0en.\nHe het \u00fea r\u00e6can me to r\u00e6denne \u00fea boc, and ic \u00fe\u00e6ron geseah mid sweartum stafum awritene ealle mine\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6don \u00fea deoflu to \u00feam Drihtnes englum \u00f0e \u00f0a lytlan boc me brohton, Hw\u00e6s abide ge her?\nGe sylfe witon \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feeos sawul is ure.\n\u00d0a englas \u00fea cw\u00e6don to \u00feam atelicum deoflum, So\u00f0 ge secga\u00f0; nima\u00f0 his sawle to \u00f0am ecum witum\nAnd \u00fea englas sona of minre syh\u00f0e gewiton.\n\u00d0a arison sona of \u00feam sweartan flocce twegen egeslice deoflu mid isenum tolum, swylce twa scearu,\n\u00d0us clypode se earming mid orwennysse, and he hra\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6s gewat to \u00f0am ecum witum butan d\u00e6dbote,\nNe fremode his gesyh\u00f0 him sylfum nan \u00feing, ac for o\u00f0rum mannum him wear\u00f0 \u00e6teowed \u00fe\u00e6t, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea\nUs s\u00e6de eac Beda be sumum gel\u00e6redum smy\u00f0e, se w\u00e6s mynsterman, and gemearcod Gode.\nSe lufode druncennysse, and dyslice leofode, and l\u00e6g on his smi\u00f0\u00f0an, and forlet his tidsangas, and \u00fea\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00f0a \u00e6t nextan geuntrumod to dea\u00f0e, and geseah helle gata him sylfum geopenode, and eac\n\u00d0a b\u00e6don \u00fea gebro\u00f0ra \u00fe\u00e6t he gebuge to Gode mid so\u00f0re behreowsunge, \u00e6r \u00fean \u00f0e he sawlode.\nHe andwyrde mid orwennysse, Hu m\u00e6g ic nu gecyrran, \u00feonne ic sylf geseah min setl on helle?\nAnd he gewat \u00fea swa mid \u00feam wordum of life, butan huslunge, and hi ne dorston him fore gebiddan.\nHim getimode \u00fea swa, swa swa us secga\u00f0 bec: \u00fe\u00e6t se \u00f0e sylfwilles nele his cyrican gesecan, \u00fe\u00e6t he\nEala, hu mycel todal is on Godes domum.\nSe eadiga Stephanus, \u00fea \u00f0a he ehtnysse \u00feolode, and to dea\u00f0e w\u00e6s gebroht for Drihtnes geleafan, \u00f0a\nAnd \u00fees earma smi\u00f0 openlice geseah \u00fea hellican wita and \u00fea hetelan deofla, \u00feyder \u00fee he, unges\u00e6lig,\nUs secga\u00f0 bec foroft \u00fe\u00e6t manega gebugon on ende, on heora for\u00f0si\u00f0e, to Gode mid f\u00e6stum geleafan,\nSe scea\u00f0a \u00fee hangode forscyldegod on rode mid andetnysse b\u00e6d Cristes arf\u00e6stnysse, and Crist him\n\u00c6lc \u00fe\u00e6ra \u00fee geortruwa\u00f0 and geenda\u00f0 butan hihte, se losa\u00f0 openlice on \u00f0am ecan forwyrde; and se \u00fee\nSe us gel\u00e6de to \u00f0am ecan life.\nAMEN.",
